# Code owners (GitHub reads this file from the default branch).
#
# THE RELEASE FILES. Everything under release/ decides what komira publishes
# and where: the release artifacts (which packages a release builds and
# ships) and the channels file (where, and with which credential). A name and
# version published to the channel is permanent, so a change here needs the
# release approver's review. The workflow that acts on them,
# .github/workflows/kci.yml, is owned the same way: it decides when a run
# publishes. So is the pull request's check, pr.yml: it decides what a pull
# request's code may reach (a tailnet node, no secret). So is the farm-connect action its build job runs: it decides
# which job joins the farm's tailnet.
#
# ⚠ PLACEHOLDER OWNER. `@komira-ai/release-approvers` is a team that does not
# exist yet: until the organisation creates it (with the release approver as
# its member, and write access to this repository), GitHub reports the line
# as an unknown owner and requires no review. Either create the team, or
# replace the handle below with the approver's own. A code-owner review is
# required only where the branch rules of main turn on "Require review from
# Code Owners".
/release/                   @komira-ai/release-approvers
/.github/workflows/kci.yml  @komira-ai/release-approvers
/.github/workflows/pr.yml   @komira-ai/release-approvers
/.github/actions/farm-connect/  @komira-ai/release-approvers
/.github/CODEOWNERS         @komira-ai/release-approvers
